### =============================================================================
### TYK MDCB ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION (CONTROL PLANE)
### =============================================================================
### Default values are set for DEVELOPMENT environments. Comments describe PRODUCTION or PERFORMANCE tuning.
###
### MDCB is the bridge between this control plane and every remote data plane.
### Data planes connect to it over RPC on 9091; it reads configuration from the
### same Redis and PostgreSQL the Dashboard uses.
### =============================================================================

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### LICENCE
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SECURITY: Supply via the gitignored .env file - never commit a licence value.
TYK_MDCB_LICENSE=${TYK_MDCB_LICENSE}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### RPC LISTENER (what the data planes connect to)
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
TYK_MDCB_LISTENPORT=9091
TYK_MDCB_HEALTHCHECKPORT=8181
TYK_MDCB_SERVEANALYTICS=true
# TYK_MDCB_HTTPPROFILE=false # Keep false; enables pprof endpoints

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### TLS
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
TYK_MDCB_USESSL=false # PROD: Set to true and supply certificates - data planes connect across networks
# TYK_MDCB_SSLCERTFILE=/etc/certs/mdcb.crt # PROD: Path to the MDCB certificate
# TYK_MDCB_SSLKEYFILE=/etc/certs/mdcb.key # PROD: Path to the MDCB private key
# TYK_MDCB_SSLINSECURESKIPVERIFY=false # PROD: Keep false to validate certificates

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### STORAGE (Redis - shared with the Dashboard)
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
TYK_MDCB_STORAGE_TYPE=redis
TYK_MDCB_STORAGE_HOST=tyk-redis
TYK_MDCB_STORAGE_PORT=6379
TYK_MDCB_STORAGE_USERNAME=
TYK_MDCB_STORAGE_PASSWORD= # SECURITY: Set a Redis password for any deployment that is not a local throwaway
TYK_MDCB_STORAGE_DATABASE=0
TYK_MDCB_STORAGE_MAXIDLE=1000
TYK_MDCB_STORAGE_MAXACTIVE=2000 # PROD/PERFORMANCE: Raise with the number of connected data planes
TYK_MDCB_STORAGE_ENABLECLUSTER=false # PROD/PERFORMANCE: Set to true for Redis Cluster
TYK_MDCB_STORAGE_USESSL=false # PROD: Set to true for secure Redis connections

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### SQL STORAGE (PostgreSQL - the Dashboard's MAIN database)
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Two things here are easy to get wrong and both fail confusingly:
###
### 1. analytics.type defaults to "mongo". Left unset, MDCB logs "no driver
###    specified for mongo, defaulting to mongo-go" and ignores every PostgreSQL
###    setting below.
### 2. This must point at the Dashboard's MAIN database (tyk_dashboard), NOT its
###    analytics database (tyk_analytics). MDCB reads `tyk_organisations` from
###    here to authorise data planes. Point it at tyk_analytics and every data
###    plane fails with "RPC Login incorrect", while MDCB logs
###    'relation "tyk_organisations" does not exist' - the gateway-side error
###    looks exactly like wrong credentials.
###
### Must match TYK_DB_STORAGE_MAIN_CONNECTIONSTRING in confs/tyk_analytics.env.
TYK_MDCB_ANALYTICSCONFIG_TYPE=postgres
TYK_MDCB_ANALYTICSCONFIG_CONNECTIONSTRING=user=tykuser password=tykSecurePass123 host=tyk-postgres port=5432 database=tyk_dashboard sslmode=disable
# SECURITY: The password above is a committed development default. Replace it, and set sslmode=require, for anything else.

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### FORWARDING & SYNCHRONISATION
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
TYK_MDCB_FORWARDANALYTICSTOPUMP=true # Let the control-plane Pump handle analytics from every data plane
TYK_MDCB_HASHKEYS=true # Must match the Gateway's TYK_GW_HASHKEYS setting on every data plane
# TYK_MDCB_SYNCWORKER_ENABLED=true # PROD: Enable so data planes keep a keyspace copy and survive a control-plane outage
# TYK_MDCB_SYNCWORKER_MAXWORKERS=2 # PROD/PERFORMANCE: Raise with the number of connected data planes
# TYK_MDCB_SYNCWORKER_MAXBATCHSIZE=100 # PROD/PERFORMANCE: Keys per sync batch
# TYK_MDCB_SYNCWORKER_TIMEBETWEENBATCHES=1 # Seconds between batches
# TYK_MDCB_SYNCWORKER_WARMUPTIME=5 # Seconds to wait before the first sync after startup

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### LOGGING
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
TYK_MDCB_LOGLEVEL=info # PROD: Set to "error" to reduce log volume
